message.content:
{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "System channel genesis block creation (U6) will be implemented as a separate public API function rather than combined with application channel creation, as permitted by the specification.",
    "The existing CreateSignedConfigUpdateEnvelope function will be renamed to SignConfigUpdateEnvelope, and the SigningIdentity interface will be extended to include both SignConfigUpdate and SignConfigUpdateEnvelope methods to encapsulate signing functionality (U8).",
    "All new config modification functions will follow the existing error handling, validation, and naming conventions of the current configtx package to maintain consistency with the existing codebase.",
    "Policy management functions for the channel group (U3) will reuse the same underlying helper utilities as policy management functions for other config groups to avoid code duplication and ensure consistent behavior.",
    "Example tests will be added to the existing example_test.go file following the project's current example structure and documentation conventions."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The existing supporting functions for retrieving dependent channel configuration fields (referenced in U1) are already fully implemented, tested, and available for use, requiring no additional development effort for these utilities.",
    "The configtx package has established, well-documented patterns for config update operations that can be followed for implementing new functions (U2, U3, U4, U5) without additional design work.",
    "The development environment has access to all required Hyperledger Fabric dependencies, test fixtures, and CI infrastructure needed for implementation and testing.",
    "No additional external dependencies or uncompleted upstream work are required to implement the features in this increment.",
    "The developer has sufficient familiarity with the existing configtx codebase to implement the features without additional ramp-up time."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Implement full channel configuration retrieval function",
      "activity_description": "Develop the public API function to retrieve the entire channel configuration as a config.Channel struct, leveraging existing pre-implemented dependent field retrieval utilities, write unit tests to validate correct config retrieval for valid configs and proper error handling for invalid configs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Implement consortium channel creation policy update function",
      "activity_description": "Develop the public API function to update the default channel creation policy value in a consortium config group, add input validation for the policy value, write unit tests for valid and invalid update scenarios, add a usage example to example_test.go.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Implement channel group policy management functions",
      "activity_description": "Develop three public API functions for adding, removing, and retrieving policies in the channel group, align implementation with existing policy management functions for other groups, write unit tests for each function, update example_test.go with usage examples for all three functions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Implement organization removal functions for config groups",
      "activity_description": "Develop three public API functions to remove an organization from consortium, application, and orderer groups respectively, add validation to prevent removal of non-existent organizations, write unit tests for each function, update example_test.go with usage examples for all three functions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Implement consortium removal function",
      "activity_description": "Develop the public API function to remove a specified consortium from the channel config, add validation to prevent removal of non-existent consortiums, write unit tests for valid and invalid removal scenarios, add a usage example to example_test.go.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Implement system channel genesis block creation function",
      "activity_description": "Develop the public API function to generate genesis blocks for system channels (excluding the application group, including only orderer and consortium groups), write unit tests to validate the genesis block structure matches system channel requirements, add a new dedicated example in example_test.go demonstrating system channel genesis block creation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Add configtx package GoDoc overview",
      "activity_description": "Write and add an Overview section to the configtx package GoDocs explaining the package's purpose, usage, and Hyperledger Fabric channel structure, ensure documentation follows standard Go doc conventions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Refactor signing identity API and update documentation",
      "activity_description": "Rename CreateSignedConfigUpdateEnvelope to SignConfigUpdateEnvelope, extend the SigningIdentity interface to include SignConfigUpdate and SignConfigUpdateEnvelope methods, update all internal references to the renamed function, update GoDocs for SigningIdentity to explain usage and differences between the two signing methods, update existing examples that use the old function name.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Regression testing and bug fixing",
      "activity_description": "Run all existing configtx package unit and integration tests to verify no regressions from new changes, fix any identified regressions or bugs found during testing.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 23
  }
}

